ACCEPT-NOTE: dc_51ka__indirect_text_references: what this case does not show: calc-engine and DNA OneCalc do not give calc_fml::evaluate a catalogue yet, so INDIRECT through them is refused as not modelled (dc-m3u); the engine is not shown the areas INDIRECT resolves and does not re-dirty a formula when a cell inside one changes (dc-m3u for INDIRECT and for dynamic reads in general); text naming a sheet the workbook lacks gives #REF! and resolves no area, so nothing records the dependency and creating that sheet later re-dirties nothing (dc-m3u); the catalogue declares no volatility, so INDIRECT is not marked volatile (cfunc-m4.1, whose volatility declaration owns it); OFFSET and the reference operators (dc-mzk) are covered by its own tests, not here

